# STASIUM XII PC: character import and wiring note (Technical Artist, updated 2026-10-03 ~20:45 ET, file-level check done)
Source: frames in /workspace/art/*_full/ checked with `tools/check_chars.py`. Full measurements are in `check_chars_report.json`. The values to wire are in `json/<char>.json`, generated by `tools/make_char_json.py`.
Scope: the PC game (Crosshaven). Wire Ironjaw v2 and Kestrel v3 now (approved). Gloam v4 needs a pivot-data fix. Bastion v4 and Mender v3 need art fixes (§7).

## 1. Import (Godot 4): spec confirmed
- Linear filter, no mipmaps, straight alpha, **Fix Alpha Border ON** (required).
  - Alpha is strictly 0/255 in all 5 sets: 0 semi-transparent px, 0 cyan, 0 near-white, 0 neon.
  - RGB under alpha 0 is black (0,0,0) everywhere. Linear filtering without Fix Alpha Border would bleed dark fringes.
  - No baked halos.
- Pack from the **per-frame PNGs**, not `strips/`. In Bastion `strips/bastion_attack_S_strip.png` and `bastion_hit_S_strip.png` are stale: an older render, ~6 px lower, different crop, does not match qa.json. Every other strip matches its frames exactly.
- 2 px padding stops atlas bleed, but it **cannot fix art already cut at the cell edge**:
  - Kestrel: hood on the top edge and cape/bow on the right edge in 112 of 176 frames.
  - Ironjaw: walk W f11 (4 px) and attack W f02 (8 px) on the left edge.
  - Mender: death N/E f04-f05 cut by the bottom edge (100 px on the last row); walk N/E f05-f06 boot on the last row.
- Use all 4 baked facings and never flip_h at runtime. But **baked does not mean painted**. Three sets ship W/N or W/E as pixel-identical flips (§4). For Mender this bakes in the staff hand swap.
- Mipmaps off at an effective scale of ~0.32 (0.5 sprite × ~0.64 board fit zoom) can shimmer a little. The shipped pawns use the same settings, so this is no regression.

## 2. Facing letters: watch the mapping
- Art uses the locked rule: S = front, walking down-right; W = front, down-left; N = back, up-left; E = back, up-right.
- The combat code (`units/pawn.gd`, origin/pc/combat-look) uses the old handoff letters. `FACING_ISO` has E=(20,10), i.e. down-right ("SE→e, SW→s, NE→n, NW→w").
- Mapping: **code e ← art S, code s ← art W, code n ← art E, code w ← art N.**
- Key the json by screen direction, or remap once at load. Don't rename files.

## 3. Pivots: centered=false, offset = -pivot (integer)
Measured sole = lowest opaque row (alpha>0.5); "+" = below the pivot. "use" is in json/<char>.json. Values in bold differ from the README/PDF.

| Char | State (cell) | File pivot | Measured sole vs pivot | Use |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ironjaw | walk/idle/attack/hit 161x155 | (78,133) | idle +5 S/W, +4 N/E. Front-foot stance +17 S/W. Torso consistent | (78,133). Optional y 137 |
| Ironjaw | death 205x178 | (102,133) | f0 = idle. S/W f04-05 body lies 41-43 px forward of the pivot | (102,133) |
| Kestrel | all but death 116x160 | (68,141) | 0 in every state and facing | (68,141) |
| Kestrel | walk S | (68,141) | soles +5..+15. Torso 6 px (f0 10 px) lower than idle | **(68,145)** optional |
| Kestrel | death 296x160 | (158,141) | 0 | (158,141) |
| Gloam | all, S / W 135x160 | (74,142) / (60,142) | **+9..+10** (pivot at the ankles, figure sinks) | **(74,151) / (60,151)** |
| Gloam | all, N / E | (74,142) / (60,142) | +1 | **(74,143) / (60,143)** |
| Gloam | death 240x160 | x S90 W149 N150 E89, y142 | same as above | **y 151 S/W, 143 N/E** |
| Bastion | walk 160x196 | (80,165) | ~+1..+6 | (80,165) |
| Bastion | idle/hit, attack 220x196 (110,165), death 330x196 (165,165) | y165 | **S +1, W +12, N +15, E +10** | **y S166 W177 N180 E175** (interim; needs art fix) |
| Mender | walk 129x183 | (64,175) | ~0 | (64,175) |
| Mender | idle/hit 129x179 S/W | (64,175) | **-7 (floats)** | **(64,168)** |
| Mender | cast 129x200 S/W | (64,196) | **-7** | **(64,189)** |
| Mender | death 230x179 S/W | x64 S, 165 W; y175 | **-7** | **y 168** |
| Mender | idle/hit/cast/death N/E | as file | -1 | as file |

- State switch at f0 (pivot-aligned): attack and cast f0 = idle for all five.
- Hit and death f0 move the torso 4-8 px while the feet stay within ~3 px. That is the authored flinch or lean, not a pivot error.
- Sorting: y-sort on the pivot (feet). Ironjaw S/W death and Mender N/E death bodies fall 30-43 px toward the camera, below the pivot. Expect them to overlap the unit in front. Acceptable for a corpse; or switch the sort key to the body centre after death f03.

