## 5. Draw scale
- All five cells were painted at one scale, normalised to Ironjaw.
- idle S f0 figure heights (cell px): Ironjaw 135, Kestrel 142, Gloam 146 (N/E 140), Bastion 138 (W 148, N 152, E 143), Mender 143 (N/E 159, incl. the staff gem).
- **Combat pawns: 0.5.** Ironjaw is then 67.5 board px, the same as today's pawn: `units/pawn.gd` L82 `SPRITE_SCALE (0.5,0.5)`. Today's 144x160 textures are centered with `SPRITE_OFFSET (0,-72)`. That centering is replaced by centered=false + offset=-pivot, with node origin = feet = tile centre.
- At 0.5 the figures stand 67-80 px tall. `HEAD_HP_Y = -76` ("clears tallest shipped figure ~68px") must become about **-84**, or be set per class (Mender N/E 80, Bastion N 76).
- **World walker: 0.46.** Ironjaw is then 62 px, which equals ironjaw_tall (189 px) × 0.33.
- Not 0.6: "game 0.6x" exists only in the contact-sheet filenames, not in the repo. At 0.6 Ironjaw is 81 px and Mender's back view 95 px, against a 64x32 tile.
- Spec source: LOOK_TARGET.md L10 row (`origin/claude/pc-zones-spec:docs/pc/LOOK_TARGET.md` line 148). One set replaces the world walker, combat pawns, action-bar portraits and class picker, and keeps the locked facing rule.
- Board refs: `board/tile.gd` 64x32 tiles. `board_view.gd` ~L1720-1740: fit zoom ~0.64.
- Picture: /workspace/luca_pics/chars/lineup.jpg.

## 6. Walk: advance frames by distance
- frame = floor(distance_along_path_cellpx / (travel_diag / 12)) mod 12, where distance_cellpx = board distance / draw_scale.
- Check on the PDF hypothesis: **only Kestrel W/E/N were measured and painted horizontal-only.** Evidence:
  - README says so.
  - Soles stay constant at 140-141.
  - The planted-foot track has dy≈0.
- Every other back/side walk already travels the 2:1 diagonal: soles rise 12-19 px through stance, foot track 20-30°, and Gloam rootmotion.json gives ±26.6° explicitly. Multiplying those by 1.118 would overshoot.

Travel per 12-frame cycle, along the drawn diagonal (cell px). The column after the arrow is board px per frame at 0.5.

| Char | S | W | N | E | board px/frame @0.5 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ironjaw | 89.2 | 89.2 | 89.2 | 89.2 | 3.72 |
| Kestrel | 129 | 128.9* | 128.9* | 128.9* | 5.37 |
| Gloam | 52.1 | 52.1 | 46.8 | 46.8 | 2.17 / 1.95 (per-frame values in gloam_full_v4_rootmotion.json; not constant) |
| Bastion | 125.06 | 115 | 115 | 115 | 5.21 / 4.79 |
| Mender | 128 | 128 | 105.8 | 105.8 | 5.33 / 4.41 |

\* Kestrel W/E/N is 115.3 horizontal × 1.118. Because those cycles have no vertical travel, the planted foot skates ~4.8 cell px per frame vertically on a diagonal move. An art fix is needed for a clean result (Kestrel is approved, so this is a note).

- The previous rows in this note were wrong for Gloam N/E (52.3), Bastion (128.6) and Mender (118.3).
- Gloam qa.json `walk4 travel_cycle_gpx 57.1` is stale (README and rootmotion say 52.1).
- Combat glide: the repo moves pawns one cell per `WALK_TILE_SEC 0.22` s, a 35.8 board px hop. At the authored cadence a hop takes 0.39-1.07 s: Ironjaw 0.56, Kestrel 0.39, Gloam 0.96/1.07, Bastion 0.40/0.44, Mender 0.39/0.47.
- Distance-driven legs at 0.22 s/hop will therefore cycle 1.8× (Kestrel) to 4.9× (Gloam) faster than authored. Design call: slow the glide (~0.4-0.5 s per hop) or accept the fast cycle.

## 7. Blocking issues before Bastion / Mender / Gloam ship
- **Gloam:** a pivot-data fix is enough (§3). S height 146 vs N 140 is a minor turn pop. Awaiting Mauro.
- **Bastion:**
  - W/N/E figures are 10-14 px taller than S, with lower feet (+10..+15) and pointed toes that read as dangling (W/N).
  - Death W/N/E f03 jumps up 12-18 px for one frame (sole 164-165 vs 177-183 on f02/f04).
  - Death S f03 lowest row 172, 6 px under the 166 floor (claim confirmed). S f04-f05 body floats above the dropped shield.
  - Idle S→walk S torso rises up to 9 px.
  - Stale strips (§1).
  - Guide: a full-plate great-helm knight is the banned "plate catalog knight" cue; steel/navy/gold is off the class palette.
- **Mender:**
  - Staff hand swap (W/N are flips).
  - S/W float 7 px (data fix in §3).
  - N/E figure 11% taller than S/W.
  - Walk N/E torso bob up to 12 px.
  - Death N/E clipped at the bottom edge. README and qa claim 0 edge touches.
  - Death S/W f05 still reads as a lump (claim confirmed).
  - Cast: the staff **no longer** covers the face (v3d). The f0→f1 pose pop remains, as the README admits.
  - Palette: mustard robe, not tide green; overlaps Ironjaw's warm family.
- **Approved sets, notes only:**
  - Kestrel edge clipping (§1). Brown/olive palette, not chalk sky / pale gold.
  - Ironjaw edge touches; dark red/iron with no ochre accent.

